# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ariane133 — a real 45nm design through the hier pipeline
#
#   133 SRAM macros, 5 hierarchy levels, 5576 nets, 111 hbundles.
#
# Run `python3 flow/ariane133/fetch.py` first: the netlist and the macro LEF
# are fetched from upstream, not checked in (see ReadMe.md).
#
# The DEF is the one already in this repo, `demo/ariane/ariane.def`.  That is
# not a convenience — it is the finding.  `opens_interchange.md` item 9
# closed by establishing that demo/ariane's LEF is an ASAP7 SRAM that was
# never the LEF for that NanGate45 DEF; the file fetched here IS its LEF, and
# the netlist fetched beside it instantiates `fakeram45_256x16` exactly 133
# times against that DEF's 133 components.  So this flow is the other half of
# that item: the same DEF, finally handed the technology that describes it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The three files below are fetched from upstream and deliberately NOT checked
# in (12 MB of somebody else's netlist, under somebody else's licence — see
# ReadMe.md).  Stated as a PRECONDITION rather than left to the importer:
# `import_def_lef` fails perfectly well on a LEF it cannot open, but its
# complaint is about a path, and the half a fresh clone needs is where the
# file comes from.  Declared up here, the run stops on line one with the
# remedy instead of after the setup that precedes the read.
require_file ariane.v fakeram45_256x16.lef NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef hint Fetch them first:  python3 flow/ariane133/fetch.py   (~12 MB, checksum-pinned; see flow/ariane133/ReadMe.md)

open_bdb ariane133.bdb

# The DEF is 2000 DBU/um and we want the placement EXACTLY, not rounded onto
# a micron grid — a 57.57 um macro is not 58 um, and the die ports are 0.07.
set_import_scale dbu
set_unit_check on

corner_margin dx 3000 dy 3000
set_min_stub_length 1000

# ── the design ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only the SRAM's LEF is needed, and that is worth knowing: the NanGate45
# standard-cell library carries a proprietary licence header, and this flow
# does not touch it.  The DEF instantiates nothing but the SRAM (it is a
# FLOORPLAN DEF), and the netlist's 76,731 standard cells are skipped as
# library cells.  The ten routing layers come from the DEF's own TRACKS.
#
# This USED to need `no_blockages`, and no longer does — item 12 landed.
# The macros' 13,034 OBS keepouts are imported and enforced; they simply no
# longer contribute Hanan loci, because each lies inside a macro whose own
# edges are already grid lines (opens_interchange.md item 12).  Grid 2.5M ->
# 6,327 cells, and the planner finishes in ~10 s instead of not at all.
#
# Consequence worth expecting: the design is now genuinely congested.  OBS
# covers metal1-metal4 across all 133 macros, so this interconnect has to
# live on metal5 and above — which is the truth about this floorplan, and
# what `no_blockages` was hiding.  The flow ends dirty; healers close most
# of it (measured: negotiate+ripup take 125 overlaps -> 61 and were still
# improving at the move budget).  Convergence here is this vehicle's own QoR
# question, not an interchange one.
# The knob that makes the obstruction model affordable here (item 12).  The
# macros' OBS keepouts are imported and enforced either way; `outside` stops
# the 13,034 of them that lie INSIDE a macro from each adding four Hanan
# lines.  Grid 2,508,972 -> 6,327 cells; the planner finishes in ~10 s
# instead of not at all.  Opt-in because it is a real trade — an interior
# locus is a reachable position (a trunk may cross a block over-the-cell) —
# and a design whose LEF draws a handful of OBS rects should not pay for a
# problem it does not have.
set_keepout_loci outside

def_layer 1 metal1 H LOW 30
def_layer 2 metal2 V LOW 30
def_layer 3 metal3 H LOW 30
def_layer 4 metal4 V LOW 30
def_layer 5 metal5 H LOW 30
def_layer 6 metal6 V LOW 30
def_layer 7 metal7 H LOW 30
def_layer 8 metal8 V LOW 30
def_layer 9 metal9 H TOP 30
def_layer 10 metal10 V TOP 30

# The TECHNOLOGY, for its track geometry alone.  The ten `def_layer` lines
# above own each layer's identity — id, name, direction, TOP/LOW, overhead —
# and `def_layer` has no syntax for PITCH or WIDTH, so those can only come
# from here.  Without it every routing layer modelled ONE FULL-PITCH signal
# slot: a wire occupying its entire track with no space beside it, zero rail
# fraction, and a "minimum wire" of 280 DBU where this technology's metal1 is
# 140.  Nothing about the ROUTE changed (one signal track per pitch either
# way, so capacity is identical — measured: 126 segments, 195 overlaps and
# 178 violations before and after), but every question about the WIDTH of a
# wire was degenerate, which is why no NDR rule could mean anything here.
#
# Composed with the DEF rather than replacing it: TRACKS below supplies the
# real track POSITIONS (pitch, offset, count) and this supplies the WIDTH.
# The two are in different units — LEF microns against DEF database units —
# and the conversion happens where the DEF's own UNITS is known.
import_lef_tech NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef

import_def_lef ../../demo/ariane/ariane.def fakeram45_256x16.lef
import_verilog ariane.v

# A DEF is flat — it lists leaf instances only — so every level between the
# die and the macros arrives from the Verilog with no geometry at all.  This
# is the step that gives them one, and the step whose warnings are the honest
# limit of this vehicle: 28 containers are placed from their macro children,
# and 16 pure-logic ones (ex_stage_i and its whole subtree, csr_regfile_i,
# id_stage_i, issue_stage_i, i_frontend, ...) have no placed descendant
# because a floorplan DEF places no standard cells — count them with
# `grep -c BUDA-1607` on the flow log.  Those 16 are why check_design is not
# clean below.
derive_container_bboxes margin 4000

# ── routing interface ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
derive_busterms 4

add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 3 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 4 skip

# ── the pipeline ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
run_hier_bundler depth 4
dump_hbundles

generate_hier_topologies
run_planner hier 2
run_nuts

check_design
report_wirelength
